B08d12 — wordexp allocation ownership and error propagation, 2026-09-28
=====================================================================

Separate, explicitly patched musl dependency supplement. This does not modify
the pinned original source or either archive, and does not close the remaining
wordexp grammar failures or increase the frozen benchmark PASS numerator.

Four source defects are repaired in the copied wordexp.c:
  - getdelim can allocate a buffer even when it returns -1 at EOF; getword must
    free that caller-owned buffer rather than losing it through the ternary.
  - a failed vector realloc must free the newly read, not-yet-inserted word.
  - failure reading the initial sentinel must distinguish EOF/syntax from a
    non-EOF allocation/read error; the latter must not become success.
  - failure allocating an empty result vector must return WRDE_NOSPACE.

The vector-growth leak is independently described by an upstream proposed
patch, not asserted here to be merged:
  https://www.openwall.com/lists/musl/2026/08/05/14
  https://www.openwall.com/lists/musl/2026/08/05/18

The fixture injects failures only into the copied wordexp translation unit via
four macro-renamed libc calls. Neither the test TU nor the rest of libc receives
these definitions. The wrappers call real getdelim/realloc/calloc/free, track
owned allocations, and force sentinel read, first word read, first/second vector
growth or empty-vector allocation failure. Normal EOF is a sixth control. Each
mode runs with all four APPEND/DOOFFS combinations. Eight checks per combination
cover status, partial count, offset, vector presence, contents/terminators,
actual fault execution, leaks after wordfree, and foreign/double free.

RED: previous transport-only patch, 12 native executions, each 192 checks with
34 failures. All builds/links succeeded; these are executed semantic failures.
GREEN: repaired patch, 12 executions, 192/192 each: 2304/2304 assertions PASS.
The matrix is GCC14/Clang19/EvoCC x O0/O2 x reference/mixed base archives.
All replacement-object link maps verify; both input archives remain unchanged.

Uninstrumented original replay was separate, with the same repair patch:
  existing transport fixture: 12 x 48/48 = 576/576 PASS;
  original functional/wordexp and functional/wordexp-static: 24/24 FAIL,
  still 71 assertion diagnostics each. The full supplement correctly returns
  FAIL. No new original-entry PASS or shell/parser repair is claimed.

